hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1542","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Sallam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash. H. Bundar told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah. H. Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari, our Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, who is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair. On the authority of Abu Muammar Abdullah ibn Sakhbra al-Azdi, on the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He wipes our shoulders in prayer and says: “Stand together, and do not differ lest your hearts differ.” Abu Masoud said: “You are more different today.” This is a comprehensive hadith, and in the hadith of Abu Usama and Ibn Abi Adi, he said: He settles our burdens. And in the hadith of Muhammad bin Jaafar, he said: He wipes our shoulders."
